     A                                  1  8'-----------------------------------
     A                                      -------------------------------'
     A                                  2  8':   M M I S   P A S S W O R D   S'
     A                                  2 42'E C U R I T Y   S Y S T E M   :'
     A                                  3  8'-----------------------------------
     A                                      -------------------------------'
     A                                  5 22'Display Program Lists and Password-
     A                                      s.'
     A                                  7  5'This function allows the user to l-
     A                                      ist all programs in the MMIS system-
     A                                      ,'
     A                                  8  2'and view any passwords which have'
     A                                  8 36'been set against them in his plant-
     A                                      .'
     A                                 10  5'Programs are sorted into five cata-
     A                                      gories based on program function:'
     A                                 11 14'UPDATE:  Programs which routinely'
     A                                 11 48'update the MMIS system.'
     A                                 12 13'INQUIRY:  On-Line Inquiry Programs-
     A                                      , Data is presented on a Terminal.'
     A                                 13 14'REPORT:  Batch Inquiry Programs, D-
     A                                      ata is sent to a Printer.'
     A                                 14  9'MAINTENANCE:  Programs to Maintain'
     A                                 14 44'the Master datasets of a Database.'
     A                                 15  1'MMIS/CSIS INTERFACE:  Programs whi-
     A                                      ch update both the MMIS and CSIS sy-
     A                                      stems.'
     A                                 17  5'The user can select one of these c-
     A                                      atagories and the programs will be'
     A                                 17 74'listed'
     A                                 18  2'with a description.  After selecti-
     A                                      ng those programs on which password-
     A                                      s are'
     A                                 19  2'desired, the program name is noted'
     A                                 19 37'and one of the other functions may'
     A                                 19 72'be'
     A                                 20  2'performed.  The "ENTER" key will d-
     A                                      isplay the next screen, and the "f2-
     A                                      " thru'
     A                                 21  2'"f5" keys will display any passwor-
     A                                      ds already set against those progra-
     A                                      ms.  The'
     A                                 22  2'"f6" key will re-display the selec-
     A                                      tion menu to change catagories.  Th-
     A                                      e "f1"'
     A                                 23  2'key returns to the main selection'
     A                                 23 36'menu.'
     A                                 23 75'HELP '
     A            COMMANDLN1    79A  B 24  1DFTVAL('f1-DISPLAY HELP f2-ADD HELP-
     A                                       f3-EXIT f4-DELETE HELP f7-HELP MEN-
     A                                      U f8-CHANGE HELP')
     A                                      DSPATR(PR)
     A  98                                  OVRDTA
     A  99        MESSAGELN1    79   M
     A  99                                  OVRDTA
     A          R VHELP2
     A                                      PUTOVR
     A                                      CF01
     A                                      CF02
     A                                      CF03
     A                                      CF04
     A                                      CF05
     A                                      CF06
     A                                      CF07
     A                                      CF08
     A                                  1  8'-----------------------------------
     A                                      -------------------------------'
     A                                  2  8':   M M I S   P A S S W O R D   S'
     A                                  2 42'E C U R I T Y   S Y S T E M   :'
     A                                  3  8'-----------------------------------
     A                                      -------------------------------'
     A                                  5 27'ADD passwords to programs.'
     A                                  7  5'The first screen allows entry of t-
     A                                      he program name noted from the prog-
     A                                      ram'
     A                                  8  2'list.  The second screen allows en-
     A                                      try of one or more password combina-
     A                                      tions'
     A                                  9  2'to be written against the program'
     A                                  9 36'named.'
     A                                 10  5'Any program with only a password e-
     A                                      ntered against it, will require the-
     A                                      '
     A                                 11  2'password by ALL users any time the'
     A                                 11 37'program is executed.'
     A                                 12  5'An entry in the SIGNON field will'
     A                                 12 39'require the password to be entered'
     A                                 12 74'by'
     A                                 13  2'any users signed on to the system'
     A                                 13 36'by that signon when the program is'
     A                                 13 71'executed.'
     A                                 14  5'An entry in the TERMINAL field wil-
     A                                      l require any users who execute the-
     A                                      '
     A                                 15  2'program from that terminal (logica-
     A                                      l device number) to enter the passw-
     A                                      ord.'
     A                                 16  5'Both SIGNON and TERMINAL may be en-
     A                                      tered to further restrict some prog-
     A                                      rams.'
     A                                 17  5'Any combination of the above may b-
     A                                      e entered against a single program'
     A                                 17 74'and as'
     A                                 18  2'many passwords as seem necessary m-
     A                                      ay be used.  Be careful, multiple'
     A                                 18 70'combination'
     A                                 19  2'passwords may require knowledge of'
     A                                 19 37'several passwords from some termin-
     A                                      al/signon'
     A                                 20  2'locations.  Enter the data desired'
     A                                 20 37'and press the "ENTER" key to write'
     A                                 20 72'it to the'
     A                                 21  2'file.  The "f5" key will display p-
     A                                      asswords already entered against th-
     A                                      e program.'
     A                                 22  2'The "f2" key will allow passwords'
     A                                 22 36'to be entered against another prog-
     A                                      ram.  The'
     A                                 23  2'"f1" key returns to the main selec-
     A                                      tion menu.'
     A                                 23 75'HELP '
     A            COMMANDLN1    79A  B 24  1DFTVAL('f1-DISPLAY HELP f2-ADD HELP-
     A                                       f3-EXIT f4-DELETE HELP f7-HELP MEN-
     A                                      U f8-CHANGE HELP')
     A                                      DSPATR(PR)
     A  98                                  OVRDTA
     A  99        MESSAGELN1    79   M
     A  99                                  OVRDTA
