     A                                      -------------------------------'
     A                                  5 15'CHANGE passwords already entered a-
     A                                      gainst programs.'
     A                                  7  5'The first screen allows entry of t-
     A                                      he program name noted from the prog-
     A                                      ram'
     A                                  8  2'list.  The second screen displays'
     A                                  8 36'the password combinations one-by-o-
     A                                      ne and'
     A                                  9  2'allows changes to be made in the f-
     A                                      ile.'
     A                                 10  5'Any program with only a password e-
     A                                      ntered against it, will require the-
     A                                      '
     A                                 11  2'password by ALL users any time the'
     A                                 11 37'program is executed.'
     A                                 12  5'An entry in the SIGNON field will'
     A                                 12 39'require the password to be entered'
     A                                 12 74'by'
     A                                 13  2'any users signed on to the system'
     A                                 13 36'by that signon when the program is'
     A                                 13 71'executed.'
     A                                 14  5'An entry in the TERMINAL field wil-
     A                                      l require any users who execute the-
     A                                      '
     A                                 15  2'program from that terminal (logica-
     A                                      l device number) to enter the passw-
     A                                      ord.'
     A                                 16  5'Both SIGNON and TERMINAL may be en-
     A                                      tered to further restrict some prog-
     A                                      rams.'
     A                                 17  5'Any combination of the above may b-
     A                                      e entered against a single program'
     A                                 17 74'and as'
     A                                 18  2'many passwords as seem necessary m-
     A                                      ay be used.  Be careful, multiple'
     A                                 18 70'combination'
     A                                 19  2'passwords may require knowledge of'
     A                                 19 37'several passwords from some termin-
     A                                      al/signon'
     A                                 20  2'locations.  Select the password to'
     A                                 20 37'be changed by pressing the "ENTER"'
     A                                 20 72'key until'
     A                                 21  2'it is displayed.  Then enter the n-
     A                                      ew data and press the "f5" key.  Th-
     A                                      e "f2" key'
     A                                 22  2'will allow passwords to be changed'
     A                                 22 37'on another program.  The "f1" key'
     A                                 22 71'returns to'
     A                                 23  2'the main selection menu.'
     A                                 23 75'HELP '
     A            COMMANDLN1    79A  B 24  1DFTVAL('f1-DISPLAY HELP f2-ADD HELP-
